# 基础词 Unit01
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit01核心词汇

{{abandon}}{{/əˈbændən}}{{v. 放弃；抛弃}}{{He abandoned his plan to study abroad due to financial difficulties.}}
{{ability}}{{/əˈbɪləti}}{{n. 能力；才能}}{{She has the ability to solve complex mathematical problems.}}
{{able}}{{/ˈeɪbl}}{{adj. 有能力的；能干的}}{{They were able to finish the project before the deadline.}}
{{abnormal}}{{/æbˈnɔːml}}{{adj. 异常的；不正常的}}{{The doctor noticed some abnormal cells in the test results.}}
{{aboard}}{{/əˈbɔːd}}{{adv./prep. 在船(车、飞机)上}}{{Welcome aboard Flight 302 to New York.}}
{{abolish}}{{/əˈbɒlɪʃ}}{{v. 废除；取消}}{{The government decided to abolish the outdated regulation.}}
{{about}}{{/əˈbaʊt}}{{prep./adv. 关于；大约}}{{The book is about the history of ancient civilizations.}}
{{above}}{{/əˈbʌv}}{{prep./adv. 在…上面；超过}}{{The temperature rose above 35 degrees yesterday.}}
{{abroad}}{{/əˈbrɔːd}}{{adv. 在国外；到国外}}{{She has been living abroad for three years.}}
{{absence}}{{/ˈæbsəns}}{{n. 缺席；不在}}{{His absence from the meeting was noticed by everyone.}}
{{absent}}{{/ˈæbsənt}}{{adj. 缺席的；不在的}}{{Three students were absent from class today.}}
{{absolute}}{{/ˈæbsəluːt}}{{adj. 绝对的；完全的}}{{I have absolute confidence in her ability to succeed.}}
{{absorb}}{{/əbˈzɔːb}}{{v. 吸收；吸引}}{{Plants absorb carbon dioxide from the atmosphere.}}
{{abstract}}{{/ˈæbstrækt}}{{adj./n. 抽象的；摘要}}{{The concept of infinity is too abstract for young children.}}
{{absurd}}{{/əbˈsɜːd}}{{adj. 荒谬的；可笑的}}{{It is absurd to believe that the earth is flat.}}
{{abuse}}{{/əˈbjuːz}}{{v./n. 滥用；虐待}}{{The report revealed the abuse of power by some officials.}}
{{academic}}{{/ˌækəˈdemɪk}}{{adj./n. 学术的；学者}}{{She published several academic papers on climate change.}}
{{accelerate}}{{/əkˈseləreɪt}}{{v. 加速；促进}}{{The government aims to accelerate economic growth.}}
{{accent}}{{/ˈæksent}}{{n. 口音；重音}}{{She speaks English with a slight French accent.}}
{{accept}}{{/əkˈsept}}{{v. 接受；承认}}{{He accepted the job offer without hesitation.}}
{{access}}{{/ˈækses}}{{n./v. 进入；通道；访问}}{{Students have access to the library 24 hours a day.}}
{{accident}}{{/ˈæksɪdənt}}{{n. 事故；意外}}{{The car accident caused a traffic jam on the highway.}}
{{accommodate}}{{/əˈkɒmədeɪt}}{{v. 容纳；提供住宿}}{{The hotel can accommodate up to 500 guests.}}
{{accompany}}{{/əˈkʌmpəni}}{{v. 陪伴；伴随}}{{She accompanied her friend to the hospital.}}
{{accomplish}}{{/əˈkʌmplɪʃ}}{{v. 完成；实现}}{{He accomplished his goal of running a marathon.}}
{{account}}{{/əˈkaʊnt}}{{n./v. 账户；描述；解释}}{{Please give us an account of what happened yesterday.}}
{{accumulate}}{{/əˈkjuːmjəleɪt}}{{v. 积累；积聚}}{{Dust had accumulated on the shelves over the months.}}
{{accurate}}{{/ˈækjərət}}{{adj. 准确的；精确的}}{{The report provides an accurate description of the situation.}}
{{accuse}}{{/əˈkjuːz}}{{v. 指控；指责}}{{He was accused of stealing money from the company.}}
{{accustom}}{{/əˈkʌstəm}}{{v. 使习惯}}{{It took her a while to accustom herself to the new environment.}}
{{achieve}}{{/əˈtʃiːv}}{{v. 达到；取得}}{{She achieved great success in her scientific research.}}
{{acknowledge}}{{/əkˈnɒlɪdʒ}}{{v. 承认；致谢}}{{He acknowledged his mistake and apologized publicly.}}
{{acquaintance}}{{/əˈkweɪntəns}}{{n. 熟人；了解}}{{He is just an acquaintance, not a close friend.}}
{{acquire}}{{/əˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 获得；学到}}{{She acquired a new skill through online courses.}}
{{adapt}}{{/əˈdæpt}}{{v. 适应；改编}}{{It is important to adapt to changing circumstances.}}
{{addict}}{{/ˈædɪkt}}{{n./v. 上瘾者；使沉溺}}{{He became addicted to playing video games.}}
{{addition}}{{/əˈdɪʃn}}{{n. 加；增加物}}{{In addition to English, she also speaks French and German.}}
{{address}}{{/əˈdres}}{{n./v. 地址；演讲；处理}}{{The president will address the nation tonight.}}
{{adequate}}{{/ˈædɪkwət}}{{adj. 足够的；适当的}}{{The supply of food is adequate for the refugees.}}
{{adjust}}{{/əˈdʒʌst}}{{v. 调整；适应}}{{You need to adjust the mirror before driving.}}
{{administer}}{{/ədˈmɪnɪstər}}{{v. 管理；执行}}{{The nurse administered the medicine to the patient.}}
{{admire}}{{/ədˈmaɪər}}{{v. 钦佩；赞赏}}{{I admire her courage and determination.}}
{{admit}}{{/ədˈmɪt}}{{v. 承认；允许进入}}{{He admitted that he had made a mistake.}}
{{adopt}}{{/əˈdɒpt}}{{v. 采用；收养}}{{The company decided to adopt a new strategy.}}
{{adult}}{{/ˈædʌlt}}{{n./adj. 成年人；成年的}}{{Adults should set a good example for children.}}
{{advance}}{{/ədˈvɑːns}}{{v./n. 前进；进步}}{{Technology continues to advance at a rapid pace.}}
{{advantage}}{{/ədˈvɑːntɪdʒ}}{{n. 优势；好处}}{{Being bilingual gives you an advantage in the job market.}}
{{adventure}}{{/ədˈventʃər}}{{n. 冒险；奇遇}}{{Traveling to Africa was a great adventure for her.}}
{{advertise}}{{/ˈædvətaɪz}}{{v. 做广告；宣传}}{{The company spent millions to advertise its new product.}}
{{advice}}{{/ədˈvaɪs}}{{n. 建议；忠告}}{{She gave me some useful advice on how to study effectively.}}
